e the Saul character the  only thing that's left is his  relationship with Kim now that she's  made a turn and they're going to be  doing something big together it really  makes me wonder if there's gonna be a  big time jump or if it's gonna end and  then that is when the time jump would  happen I'm not considering Jean in that  at all though because Jean is a whole  different question how much time do we  actually think we're gonna spend with  Jean that's another assumption that fans  have had was that in wrapping up Jean  story which I definitely think they'll  do a lot of fans thought that they would  have full jean episodes that take place  in that timeline at this point what  happens to Jean is one of the biggest  mysteries left to answer I don't think  they can do that in a single teaser at  the beginning of the season nor would it  make sense to answer that question at  the beginning of the season in most  scenarios so will there be a lot of Jean  time or is that something they can just  wrap up in a couple of short sequences  when we talk about timelines and how  much time is going to pass another  question I would have is will season six  have any major cameos from Breaking Bad  characters I think there's a distinct  possibility that they might bring Hank  and Gomi back their connection to crazy  eight Crazy Eights connection to the  cartel story there's definitely room to  bring them in in a meaningful way most  people wonder if Walter White or Jesse  Pinkman will show up I'm not really sure  the showrunner Peter Gould has said on  numerous occasions since El Camino came  out it took the pressure off better call  Saul in other words it didn't need to  show them because they had one more  scene in El Camino he brings up two  important points and I think this is how  they'll decide the first is they're  telling the story of Jimmy's  transformation so if using Jesse or Walt  would serve that story then they would  think about doing it in other words  they're 