ng they knew for certain but they  do know more about these characters than  we do from portraying them so I think we  will be learning a lot more about that  in season six but it's hard to say if  that has an impact on how she's going to  leave I'm really glad that they decided  to make Howard the target of this it  keeps that side of the story alive one  of the best things that season 5 did was  bring all the stories together and when  she quit Mesa Verde it almost felt like  the lawyer side of the story was just  not going to be important anymore  Plus Howard keeps the connection with  Chuck in the mix and Jimmy's inability  to deal with his death even though his  latest trauma from the shootout has  taken center stage  Chuck's death still haunts Jimmy Howard  being in the story keeps that viable as  a pressure point for him so I'm glad  that's there and I'm definitely curious  to see what they cook up and for Kim I'm  curious to know how long she's been  thinking about doing something like this  I don't think she's trying to scam Jimmy  out of the money that's something I saw  a lot of in the comments that people  thought that she was playing a long game  that seems like a little bit of a  stretch but what's great about where  we're at right now is we really don't  know for four seasons the mystery was  how does this guy Jimmy McGill who is  generally good hearted but is also a con  man who even when he tries to play it  straight has a propensity to cut corners  and bend the rules how does this guy  become no ethics style Saul Goodman now  the mystery is much more about Kim who  she is where she coming from with this  new direction and how is it gonna be the  wedge that gets between them or is it  just gonna be a temporary setback is  what they're getting into now with  Howard is that just gonna sideline the  relationship we do have that mention of  a phone call that Saul talks to  Francesca about in that flash forward to  the Breaking Bad timeline so they may  